    "sections": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Logan's Run epitomizes 1970s sci-fi's gleaming retro-futurism, following the sterile utopian/dystopian path carved by <a href=\"/movie/636\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"636\">THX 1138</a> (1971). The film's premise - mandatory death at 30 to maintain population control - taps into 1970s anxieties about youth culture and environmental collapse. Its practical effects and elaborate sets created a distinctive aesthetic that influenced later works like <a href=\"/movie/97\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"97\">TRON</a> (1982) and <a href=\"/movie/1635\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"1635\">The Island</a> (2005). The domed city's mix of hedonism and hidden tyranny became a blueprint for countless dystopian futures."
      },
      {
