      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The film's exploration of age-based social control resonates with other 70s sci-fi classics like <a href=\"/movie/11484\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"11484\">Rollerball</a> (1975) and <a href=\"/movie/13282\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"13282\">Death Race 2000</a> (1975), which similarly questioned authority through violent spectacle. Michael York's transformation from enforcer to rebel established a character arc later echoed in <a href=\"/movie/7299\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"7299\">Equilibrium</a> (2002) and <a href=\"/movie/1635\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"1635\">The Island</a> (2005) - the system's perfect soldier becoming its greatest threat."
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "The production design by Dale Hennesy merges modernist architecture with psychedelic color schemes, creating spaces that feel both futuristic and distinctly 1970s. This retro-future aesthetic influenced everything from <a href=\"/movie/68\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"68\">Brazil</a> (1985) to <a href=\"/movie/70160\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"70160\">The Hunger Games</a> (2012). The practical effects, while dated, showcase ingenious pre-CGI filmmaking techniques that gave the film its tangible, lived-in quality. SUBHEAD: Legacy and Influence"
      },
      {
