      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Despite its dated elements, Logan's Run pioneered several sci-fi tropes that became genre staples. The concept of enforced population control influenced films like <a href=\"/movie/9693\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"9693\">Children of Men</a> (2006) and <a href=\"/movie/49530\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"49530\">In Time</a> (2011). Its blend of hedonistic pleasure and hidden horror prefigured the false utopias of <a href=\"/movie/603\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"603\">The Matrix</a> (1999) and <a href=\"/movie/27260\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"27260\">Brave New World</a> (2020). The Sandman protocol - hunting one's own kind - became a recurring theme in films like <a href=\"/movie/78\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"78\">Blade Runner</a> (1982) and <a href=\"/movie/180\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"180\">Minority Report</a> (2002)."
      }
